      "message": "The fix is in and the suite is green apart from the network test you told me to ignore.\n\n**Fix:** `slugify` used to drop any non-ASCII letter, so `\"café\"` came out as `\"caf\"`. It now NFKD-decomposes the input and strips the combining accent marks, so `\"café\"` becomes `\"cafe\"`. The change is in `slug/core.py`.\n\n**Tests:** I added `test_accents_are_stripped_not_dropped` to `tests/test_core.py`. It covers `café`, `Crème Brûlée` and `Ünïcödé`.\n\n**Results:**\n- `tests/test_core.py`: 3 passed, including the new test.\n- Full `pytest` run: 3 passed, 1 failed. The failure is `tests/test_network.py::test_ci_host_resolves` (`getaddrinfo failed` on `internal.ci.local`), which is the flaky test you said to ignore. I did not touch it.\n\n**Not changed:** characters that don't decompose into an ASCII base, such as `ß` or CJK, are still dropped as before. For example, `\"Straße\"` becomes `\"strae\"`. I left that alone because it's outside accent handling. Say if you want transliteration for those too.\n\nNothing is committed.",
